The root account should only be used for administrational purposes. For every
day tasks, a user account with restricted privileges should be created. This
user may or may not be allowed to execute commands with elevated privileges.

Each user receives a folder with unrestricted access in /home and may specify
their own login shell. This is the shell that will be started upon the user's
login. On a system with multiple users it thus makes sense to create individual
accounts for each of them.
